\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Layer 4 drawn rather than argued. The released head asked for three objects emits three place points, $14.5$ and $13.0$\,cm from the basket. The basket itself is \emph  {not} fixed --- it is re-placed every episode, with a per-task diameter of $3.66$\,cm (max $3.96$) --- so a memorised place point is wrong by $14$\,cm against a target that only ever moves by $4$, and $14$\,cm is enough to release a grocery over open table. Radial distances are measured; angles are for legibility.}}{10}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:placepoint}{{4}{10}{Layer 4 drawn rather than argued. The released head asked for three objects emits three place points, $14.5$ and $13.0$\,cm from the basket. The basket itself is \emph {not} fixed --- it is re-placed every episode, with a per-task diameter of $3.66$\,cm (max $3.96$) --- so a memorised place point is wrong by $14$\,cm against a target that only ever moves by $4$, and $14$\,cm is enough to release a grocery over open table. Radial distances are measured; angles are for legibility}{figure.caption.24}{}}
